  "sourceInterpretation": "Original official image identifies ESP-IDFv6.1-dirty; its exact private source revision is unknown. Fixed public fff9895c82d744c7237be8847347bdd1b07c6643 provides the register/event definitions and driver sequence. mspi_periph.c assigns source112 to systemMSPI2 and irq=-1 to peripheralMSPI3. No extra MSPI3 line is inferred.",
  "semantics": {
    "registers": "System INT_ENA/CLR/RAW/ST at205020c0/c4/c8/cc. Documented mask0xfc0023f8. RAW is independent of ENA; only paired CLR clears actual events. Reset clears controller banks but preserves external supplied mode/data.",
    "events": "An executed access with an invalid PSRAM MMU entry raises readbit7 or writebit9 and retains the synchronous access fault. Fetch is a read. Valid mapping beyond explicit backing,unsupported sensitive/alternate targets,power/cache/pad gating are not falsely converted into address-error events. First-failure order is preserved across page boundaries; rejected cross-page writes remain atomic.",
    "routing": "Only real masked system events feed source112,per-hart matrix and CLIC. Local MSPI3 command-completion RAW remains separate and no nonzero peripheral IRQ enable is accepted without a demonstrated route.",
    "unsupported": [
      "ECC and XTS engines",
      "MSPI FIFO underrun/overflow and asynchronous timing",
      "Controller-local PMS windows",
      "AXI Flash-write event on alternate target",
      "MSPI3 interrupt route",
      "Physical RAM die identification",
      "Complete INK4 Plus board/display"
    ]
  },
